  "about": "Language-neutral test vectors for the personal ledger's fixed rules. The Python side (api/app/modules/personal/ledger_rules.py and migration 0013's backfill, tests/api/test_personal_backfill.py) and the Dart port (app/lib/core/finance/) must both pass every case. Amounts are minor units (paise). opening_balance: the opening balance that makes an account's derived balance, right after its first entry with a reported balance, equal that balance; 0 for credit_card and loan accounts (card SMS report a limit, not what's owed) and when no entry reported one. 'entries' are the account's live entries in its currency, listed in any order; they're sorted by (day, at, created_at, id), where 'at' is when the bank's SMS arrived, else created_at. A null balance_minor means the entry reported none. There are no adjustments: the backfill never sees one. account_ids: uuid5(namespace, '<user_id>|<label>'), the id every phone and the backfill give a bank SMS label's account. account_types: the type that account gets ('credit card' in the label, in any case, makes a credit_card; anything else is a bank account). plan_ids: uuid5(plan_namespace, '<income id>|<rule id>'), the id the app gives the plan a rule makes for an income (api/app/modules/personal/ledger_rules.py plan_id), so a replay or a re-read SMS makes no second plan. reminder_state_ids: uuid5(reminder_namespace, '<user id>|<dedup key>'), the id of your decision on a reminder (ledger_rules.reminder_state_id), so two devices deciding about one reminder write one row.",
